  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_q7.c **** /**
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_q7.c ****  * @param[in]   *S points to an instance of the Q7 FIR filter structure.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_q7.c ****  * @param[in]   *pSrc points to the block of input data.
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_q7.c ****  * @param[out]  *pDst points to the block of output data.
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_q7.c ****  * @param[in]   blockSize number of samples to process per call.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_q7.c ****  * @return 	none.
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_q7.c ****  *
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_q7.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_q7.c ****  * \par
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_q7.c ****  * The function is implemented using a 32-bit internal accumulator.
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_q7.c ****  * Both coefficients and state variables are represented in 1.7 format and multiplications yield a 
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_q7.c ****  * The 2.14 intermediate results are accumulated in a 32-bit accumulator in 18.14 format.
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_q7.c ****  * There is no risk of internal overflow with this approach and the full precision of intermediate 
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_q7.c ****  * The accumulator is converted to 18.7 format by discarding the low 7 bits.
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_q7.c ****  * Finally, the result is truncated to 1.7 format.
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_q7.c ****  */
